{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00398",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.37,
      "end_seconds": 4.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.61,
      "end_seconds": 9.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.89,
      "end_seconds": 19.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details. We came because of a dry cough that won't go away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.57,
      "end_seconds": 22.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.91,
      "end_seconds": 29.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "It's been about three months now. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.61,
      "end_seconds": 36.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.15,
      "end_seconds": 46.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.13,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. Sipping water helps a bit. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.28,
      "end_seconds": 50.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.21,
      "end_seconds": 72.14,
      "duration_seconds": 20.93,
      "text": "It usually comes with a burning in the chest after meals. The burning in the chest after meals? That's been for about a year. As for burning in the chest after meals, it comes and goes. I've also had a sour taste in the mouth, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.78,
      "end_seconds": 74.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Any shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.77,
      "end_seconds": 79.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Hmm, no, I haven't had any shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.63,
      "end_seconds": 84.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any wheezing, night sweats or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.74,
      "end_seconds": 88.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I haven't had wheezing, night sweats or trouble swallowing, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.13,
      "end_seconds": 94.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.19,
      "end_seconds": 100.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "I haven't had weight loss or coughing up blood, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.01,
      "end_seconds": 104.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.76,
      "end_seconds": 106.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.48,
      "end_seconds": 122.85,
      "duration_seconds": 15.37,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.84,
      "end_seconds": 127.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 128.5,
      "end_seconds": 138.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 78, temperature is 36.6 degrees. BP is 116 over 70, respiratory rate 16, oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.7,
      "end_seconds": 142.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.23,
      "end_seconds": 148.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Yes, I had a knee arthroscopy, three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.2,
      "end_seconds": 151.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.17,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I'm on losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 157.02,
      "end_seconds": 165.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the losartan was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.3,
      "end_seconds": 169.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.18,
      "end_seconds": 179.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Asthalin inhaler. I take it when needed. Digene. I take it after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.6,
      "end_seconds": 182.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.59,
      "end_seconds": 185.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "About three months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.32,
      "end_seconds": 189.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.64,
      "end_seconds": 200.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure, for about a year. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.25,
      "end_seconds": 201.95,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.69,
      "end_seconds": 208.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Asthma, for two years. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.48,
      "end_seconds": 211.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.21,
      "end_seconds": 220.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for about ten years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.48,
      "end_seconds": 241.24,
      "duration_seconds": 19.76,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the acid reflux in your file as well. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.42,
      "end_seconds": 244.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.06,
      "end_seconds": 251.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.41,
      "end_seconds": 258.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.12,
      "text": "Pollen. I come out in... well, sneezing. Yes, ibuprofen. I get stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.16,
      "end_seconds": 274.37,
      "duration_seconds": 13.21,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.8,
      "end_seconds": 279.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Good, uh, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.38,
      "end_seconds": 286.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.47,
      "end_seconds": 289.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.88,
      "end_seconds": 303.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Chest is clear and the throat looks a little red at the back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.41,
      "end_seconds": 305.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.09,
      "end_seconds": 333.96,
      "duration_seconds": 24.87,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Putting it all together, my working impression is a cough driven by acid reflux. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be cough-variant asthma, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.58,
      "end_seconds": 336.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.58,
      "end_seconds": 360.08,
      "duration_seconds": 20.5,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a cough driven by acid reflux do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a dry cough that won't go away for about three months, severe, and no coughing up blood or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.64,
      "end_seconds": 362.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.95,
      "end_seconds": 370.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Let's get a chest X-ray, for chronic cough. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.33,
      "end_seconds": 373.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.68,
      "end_seconds": 398.69,
      "duration_seconds": 24.01,
      "text": "I'm going to order breathing tests, for chronic cough. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'd like you to take pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, for four weeks. You take it by mouth. That's for reflux. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Don't eat for two or three hours before lying down, and raise the head of the bed a little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.22,
      "end_seconds": 411.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "Okay. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.11,
      "end_seconds": 413.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.05,
      "end_seconds": 423.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 425.07,
      "end_seconds": 428.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.99,
      "end_seconds": 436.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 437.45,
      "end_seconds": 444.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "So, I take the pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.95,
      "end_seconds": 450.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.94,
      "end_seconds": 453.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "I appreciate your time, doctor."
    }
  ]
}